    "['ipv6 unicast-routing', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set routing-options router-id 0.0.0.0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set routing-options router-id 0.0.0.0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset routing-options router-id 0.0.0.0\\nset protocols router-advertisement interface all\\nset forwarding-options family inet6 mode packet-based\\n##\\n\\nNote: The Juniper equivalent for enabling IPv6 routing is more complex than a single command. The above combination:\\n1. Sets a router ID (required for IPv6 routing)\\n2. Enables router advertisements (for IPv6 neighbor discovery)\\n3. Configures packet-based forwarding for IPv6 (equivalent to Cisco's ipv6 unicast-routing)\\n\\nThis is the closest functional equivalent in Junos, though the implementation details differ from Cisco's single command approach.\", 'trans_template': 'set routing-options router-id 0.0.0.0'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols router-advertisement interface all', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols router-advertisement interface all', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset routing-options router-id 0.0.0.0\\nset protocols router-advertisement interface all\\nset forwarding-options family inet6 mode packet-based\\n##\\n\\nNote: The Juniper equivalent for enabling IPv6 routing is more complex than a single command. The above combination:\\n1. Sets a router ID (required for IPv6 routing)\\n2. Enables router advertisements (for IPv6 neighbor discovery)\\n3. Configures packet-based forwarding for IPv6 (equivalent to Cisco's ipv6 unicast-routing)\\n\\nThis is the closest functional equivalent in Junos, though the implementation details differ from Cisco's single command approach.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols router-advertisement interface all'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set forwarding-options family inet6 mode packet-based', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set forwarding-options family inet6 mode packet-based', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset routing-options router-id 0.0.0.0\\nset protocols router-advertisement interface all\\nset forwarding-options family inet6 mode packet-based\\n##\\n\\nNote: The Juniper equivalent for enabling IPv6 routing is more complex than a single command. The above combination:\\n1. Sets a router ID (required for IPv6 routing)\\n2. Enables router advertisements (for IPv6 neighbor discovery)\\n3. Configures packet-based forwarding for IPv6 (equivalent to Cisco's ipv6 unicast-routing)\\n\\nThis is the closest functional equivalent in Junos, though the implementation details differ from Cisco's single command approach.\", 'trans_template': 'set forwarding-options family inet6 mode packet-based'}]]": 1,
