    "['ipv6 enable', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet6', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `ipv6 enable` command:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet6\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, you would need to apply this to each interface (ge-1/0/0, ge-1/0/1, ge-1/0/2 in this case) to match the Cisco configuration. The Juniper command enables IPv6 processing on the interface by adding the `inet6` family to the interface configuration.\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet6'}]]": 1,
